# Product scope

Barbershop booking SaaS MVP. Solo developer, shipping toward first paying customers, not
toward a large-team-scale architecture. Source of truth for scope: `EXECUTION-PLAN.md` and
`prisma/schema.prisma`. If a request seems to go beyond what's in those files, say so and
ask before building it — don't silently expand scope.

**Decision recorded:** single codebase, single architecture. Target = barber shops + hair salons only. Differentiation is terminology, branding, and demo seed data. No new domain entities (`Resource`, `Room`, `Equipment` all deferred).

**The target is barber shops and hair salons. Nothing else.**

**Do not build anything listed as excluded in `EXECUTION-PLAN.md`** (staff login,
SMS/WhatsApp, payments, multi-location, analytics, customer accounts, ~~i18n~~, marketplace
features, POS/inventory) unless explicitly asked to start that phase.

What's excluded entirely for now: Staff login, SMS/WhatsApp reminders, deposits/payments, multi-location,
analytics dashboard, customer accounts, ~~i18n~~, recurring/subscription
bookings, reviews or any marketplace surface, POS/inventory, granular
permissions beyond Owner/Staff, `Resource`/rooms/bays/equipment, any
vertical beyond barber shops and hair salons, custom domains, wildcard
subdomains.

When in doubt about scope, ask. A clarifying question costs a few seconds; unwinding
unwanted scope costs an afternoon.

## Planned and in scope — do not re-add as exclusions

This section exists because an earlier session invented two exclusions that were
never decided ("No dark mode", "No drag-to-select on the calendar"). Neither
phrase ever appeared in `EXECUTION-PLAN.md`, `V1-LAUNCH-PLAN.md`, or `CLAUDE.md`.
Both features are planned. They were removed from this file on 13 Aug 2026.

**Phase 15a** — runs after the Phase 15 security audit, before the salon vertical:

- **i18n** — German default with an English toggle. Scope is a default locale plus
  a toggle only: *not* locale-routed URLs, per-tenant language settings, or a
  translation-management service, which do remain excluded.
- **Light/dark mode toggle** — constraints are already recorded in the code at
  `globals.css:71-74`, `globals.css:13`, and `field.tsx:60`. Read them before
  starting.
- **Drag-to-select booking on the calendar** — Outlook/Google Calendar-style range
  selection. On touch it must be long-press, never plain drag, because plain drag
  collides with the scroll gesture.

**Phase 16a** — the landing page, deliberately last, after the salon vertical. It
is a link to leave behind after an in-person pitch, not an SEO or
organic-discovery surface.

Committed in `f1d73e9`. The authoritative records are "Decisions recorded after
14.3" in `EXECUTION-PLAN.md` and the Phase 15a/16a sections in
`V1-LAUNCH-PLAN.md`. If those files and this one ever disagree, they win.

**Note on the exclusion lists above:** `i18n` appears in both of them struck
through, matching `EXECUTION-PLAN.md`. It was reversed from "excluded entirely" to
Phase 15a in `f1d73e9`. Struck rather than deleted, deliberately — a list that
quietly drops its own reversals stops being a record of what was decided, and the
strike is what tells a future session this was reconsidered rather than never
considered. Everything else on those lists stands and is still excluded.
